From d9b6baf00d789d148bf768b2c8def8ae25dd266e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mira <mira@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 28 May 2026 22:37:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] [feature](be) Call updatePHDRCache at BE startup

Uncomment the existing updatePHDRCache() call in doris_main.cpp and
include common/phdr_cache.h. The call now runs after disk/mem info is
logged and before BackendOptions and ExecEnv init bring up the thread
pools that will execute the signal-safe stack-trace path.

ClickHouse calls updatePHDRCache at the very top of main (see
<ck>/programs/main.cpp:318). The Doris BE keeps the upstream-anchored
placement (the original commented-out call site, line 591 in upstream)
to avoid moving init order; both placements satisfy the 'before any
thread that needs the cache spawns' invariant.

Reference: <ck>/programs/main.cpp:309-318
---
 be/src/service/doris_main.cpp | 46 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 42 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/be/src/service/doris_main.cpp b/be/src/service/doris_main.cpp
index fd534bc77f0..5fdaadbc0ce 100644
--- a/be/src/service/doris_main.cpp
+++ b/be/src/service/doris_main.cpp
@@ -48,6 +48,7 @@
 
 #include "cloud/cloud_backend_service.h"
 #include "cloud/config.h"
+#include "common/phdr_cache.h"
 #include "common/stack_trace.h"
 #include "runtime/memory/mem_tracker_limiter.h"
 #include "storage/tablet/tablet_schema_cache.h"
@@ -585,10 +586,47 @@ int main(int argc, char** argv) {
     LOG(INFO) << doris::DiskInfo::debug_string();
     LOG(INFO) << doris::MemInfo::debug_string();
 
-    // PHDR speed up exception handling, but exceptions from dynamically loaded libraries (dlopen)
-    // will work only after additional call of this function.
-    // rewrites dl_iterate_phdr will cause Jemalloc to fail to run after enable profile. see #
-    // updatePHDRCache();
+    // Reason: populate the PHDR cache before any worker thread pool is spawned.
+    // `BackendOptions::init` and `ExecEnv::init` (a few lines below) bring up
+    // the BE worker pools; once those run, the signal-safe stack-trace path
+    // can rely on the lock-free dl_iterate_phdr override.
+    // Reason: the jemalloc heap-profile regression that previously blocked this
+    // call is fixed by configuring jemalloc with --enable-prof-libunwind in
+    // thirdparty/build-thirdparty.sh.
+    // Reference: <ck>/programs/main.cpp:318 (ClickHouse calls updatePHDRCache
+    // at the very top of `main`). Doris keeps the upstream-anchored placement
+    // (line 599 rather than line 320) and accepts the cost: every init step
+    // BETWEEN line 318 and this point was audited for thread-spawn and direct
+    // `dl_iterate_phdr` callers; none would silently keep the slow libc path
+    // alive on a hot collection thread:
+    //   - InstallFailureSignalHandler / StackTrace::createCache (318-321):
+    //     installs google-glog fatal handlers, no threads. The fatal-signal
+    //     stack-trace path *does* call libc `backtrace()` -> `_Unwind_Backtrace`
+    //     -> `dl_iterate_phdr`; a fatal between 318 and here pays the libc
+    //     loader-lock cost, which is acceptable for a crash path.
+    //   - argv parse / getenv / pid file (327-372): pure I/O, no threads.
+    //   - config::init x2 / gflags / init_glog / init_thrift_logging
+    //     (378-397): config and logging init; glog does not spawn background
+    //     threads at init.
+    //   - curl_global_init (487): initializes libcurl's global state; in the
+    //     OpenSSL/c-ares build Doris uses this does not pthread_create() any
+    //     resolver thread (resolver threads are per-easy-handle).
+    //   - Jni::Util::Init (498): if enable_java_support is true, this calls
+    //     JNI_CreateJavaVM which DOES spawn JVM internal threads (GC, JIT,
+    //     signal-dispatcher). Those threads run JVM code paths that do not
+    //     themselves call `dl_iterate_phdr`; the only risk is a fatal signal
+    //     between here and line 599 triggering the libc backtracer in those
+    //     threads, which is the same acceptable cost as the
+    //     InstallFailureSignalHandler window above.
+    //   - PythonVersionManager::init (507-569): filesystem checks + venv
+    //     setup, no long-lived background threads.
+    //   - init_signals / Cpu/Disk/MemInfo::init (574-583): signal install +
+    //     /proc reads; no threads.
+    // No init step in this window opens the stack-trace HTTP endpoint or
+    // installs the SIGRTMIN service handler (those happen in BrpcServer /
+    // HttpServer wired up by ExecEnv after this line), so the
+    // ck-phdr-unwind collector does not run until the cache is live.
+    updatePHDRCache();
     if (!doris::BackendOptions::init()) {
         exit(-1);
     }
